WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.199
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:05.030 --> 00:00:07.580
SPEAKER: Every organization
would like their API program

00:00:07.580 --> 00:00:09.320
to be successful.

00:00:09.320 --> 00:00:12.710
Quality assurance strategy is
about detecting and correcting

00:00:12.710 --> 00:00:16.940
problems during the SDLC
to ensure APIs are reliable

00:00:16.940 --> 00:00:19.160
and consumers can
utilize them to deliver

00:00:19.160 --> 00:00:21.960
high-quality
digital experiences.

00:00:21.960 --> 00:00:24.050
Let's look at the digital
value chain again.

00:00:24.050 --> 00:00:27.530
Consider where quality
assurance should be implemented.

00:00:27.530 --> 00:00:29.360
In most organizations,
we quickly

00:00:29.360 --> 00:00:31.790
identify the technical areas.

00:00:31.790 --> 00:00:35.750
Your back-end servers and
APIs must be clear of defects

00:00:35.750 --> 00:00:38.390
to ensure you are
generating great and quality

00:00:38.390 --> 00:00:40.020
digital experiences.

00:00:40.020 --> 00:00:43.220
However, focusing solely on
protecting code integrity

00:00:43.220 --> 00:00:46.160
is only the start of a
quality assurance strategy.

00:00:46.160 --> 00:00:48.530
Your team should
actively participate

00:00:48.530 --> 00:00:52.070
and have a culture of continuous
quality assurance as well.

00:00:52.070 --> 00:00:54.860
Developers and key team
members must consistently

00:00:54.860 --> 00:00:59.060
strive to find, prevent,
and correct issues.

00:00:59.060 --> 00:01:02.360
Quality assurance should also be
an active process in deploying

00:01:02.360 --> 00:01:04.400
your connected experiences.

00:01:04.400 --> 00:01:07.100
This can be automated through
a continuous integration

00:01:07.100 --> 00:01:08.900
and delivery tools
that could also

00:01:08.900 --> 00:01:11.450
help with unit testing,
integration testing,

00:01:11.450 --> 00:01:13.190
and performance testing.

00:01:13.190 --> 00:01:15.560
The principle of
automation and quality

00:01:15.560 --> 00:01:18.410
is an essential part of
digital transformation.

00:01:18.410 --> 00:01:22.370
CI/CD often helps reduce
rework and technical debt,

00:01:22.370 --> 00:01:24.740
while maintaining quality
throughout the entire

00:01:24.740 --> 00:01:26.390
development lifecycle.

00:01:26.390 --> 00:01:30.110
Some of the benefits of CI/CD,
with the help of automation,

00:01:30.110 --> 00:01:33.200
include increasing the
speed of finding and fixing

00:01:33.200 --> 00:01:35.990
code and integration
errors, decrease

00:01:35.990 --> 00:01:38.780
in the cost of finding
and fixing those errors,

00:01:38.780 --> 00:01:42.440
increase in dev team's
confidence in code stability,

00:01:42.440 --> 00:01:44.840
increase in dev team's
frequency in releasing

00:01:44.840 --> 00:01:46.220
the code to production.

00:01:46.220 --> 00:01:48.560
But successful quality
assurance strategies

00:01:48.560 --> 00:01:51.200
must also occur at
the customer level.

00:01:51.200 --> 00:01:53.990
Leveraging your customers
to receive feedback, test

00:01:53.990 --> 00:01:57.260
new features and services,
and validate user experiences

00:01:57.260 --> 00:02:00.860
must be an integral part of your
continuous improvement process

00:02:00.860 --> 00:02:03.530
and ensure that your
organization is able to keep

00:02:03.530 --> 00:02:05.000
your customers happy.

00:02:05.000 --> 00:02:08.539
Let's take a look at the details
within quality assurance.

00:02:08.539 --> 00:02:10.550
Here are a few
factors to consider

00:02:10.550 --> 00:02:13.280
when building your quality
assurance strategy.

00:02:13.280 --> 00:02:16.820
Reducing risks is critical
in your QA strategy.

00:02:16.820 --> 00:02:19.250
The risk of a bad experience
reaching the customer

00:02:19.250 --> 00:02:22.400
can be greatly reduced
when regression testing

00:02:22.400 --> 00:02:25.470
and continuous quality
assurance is in place.

00:02:25.470 --> 00:02:27.410
Be sure that your
team understands

00:02:27.410 --> 00:02:29.990
what the objectives,
requirements, and acceptance

00:02:29.990 --> 00:02:33.680
criteria are for new features
and changes to your APIs.

00:02:33.680 --> 00:02:35.960
The key is to make sure your
requirements are clearly

00:02:35.960 --> 00:02:40.340
aligned with your business needs
and stakeholders' expectations.

00:02:40.340 --> 00:02:43.250
Does your team have the right
technical skills and capacity

00:02:43.250 --> 00:02:45.830
to ensure quality
assurance is being met?

00:02:45.830 --> 00:02:48.620
As testing becomes
increasingly automated,

00:02:48.620 --> 00:02:51.710
QA engineers are replacing
manual testing efforts.

00:02:51.710 --> 00:02:54.530
Your API team and
testers should automation

00:02:54.530 --> 00:02:57.260
testing and QA skills
as well as understanding

00:02:57.260 --> 00:02:59.900
of the key test frameworks
in the development cycle.

00:02:59.900 --> 00:03:02.030
Understand how
your products work

00:03:02.030 --> 00:03:04.040
and how the tools
can be used to help

00:03:04.040 --> 00:03:06.260
maintain your quality assurance.

00:03:06.260 --> 00:03:10.580
Each tool in your CI/CD process,
along with your API platform,

00:03:10.580 --> 00:03:13.550
can be leveraged in
your QA strategies.

00:03:13.550 --> 00:03:15.650
The business must
support a culture

00:03:15.650 --> 00:03:19.020
of quality assurance and
continuous improvement as well.

00:03:19.020 --> 00:03:22.550
This means including QA further
upstream in the requirements

00:03:22.550 --> 00:03:25.610
and design process
and also collaboration

00:03:25.610 --> 00:03:29.180
between the product on the QA
to mutually define acceptance

00:03:29.180 --> 00:03:31.170
criteria and test cases.

00:03:31.170 --> 00:03:34.970
Finally, also consider any
organizational regulations

00:03:34.970 --> 00:03:36.530
that are required.

00:03:36.530 --> 00:03:40.760
These may also drive quality and
may require specific standards

00:03:40.760 --> 00:03:43.190
to satisfy feature release.

00:03:43.190 --> 00:03:44.900
Having your
regulations understood

00:03:44.900 --> 00:03:48.410
by everyone on your team
will prevent needless cycles

00:03:48.410 --> 00:03:50.550
to approve new features.

00:03:50.550 --> 00:03:53.510
So let's summarize everything
with a few key strategies

00:03:53.510 --> 00:03:57.020
to build quality into your SDLC.

00:03:57.020 --> 00:04:00.350
The first is to
make time to test.

00:04:00.350 --> 00:04:04.520
Unfortunately, some teams often
look to QA as an afterthought.

00:04:04.520 --> 00:04:07.100
Only when something breaks
does the question come up,

00:04:07.100 --> 00:04:08.990
where was our quality assurance?

00:04:08.990 --> 00:04:13.490
Have dedicated time and QA role
embedded in your daily routine

00:04:13.490 --> 00:04:16.760
to test your APIs
and validate quality.

00:04:16.760 --> 00:04:19.850
Second, everyone is
responsible for quality.

00:04:19.850 --> 00:04:22.130
As we discussed
earlier, everyone

00:04:22.130 --> 00:04:24.335
is responsible throughout
your digital value chain

00:04:24.335 --> 00:04:26.060
and software
development lifecycle

00:04:26.060 --> 00:04:29.810
to test, detect, prevent,
and correct issues.

00:04:29.810 --> 00:04:32.240
Do not hand off QA
to someone else.

00:04:32.240 --> 00:04:34.820
Follow through on every issue.

00:04:34.820 --> 00:04:39.160
Third, documentation
is essential.

00:04:39.160 --> 00:04:41.500
The more your team gets
comfortable with documenting

00:04:41.500 --> 00:04:43.960
product features
and product issues,

00:04:43.960 --> 00:04:46.180
the better your
quality will get.

00:04:46.180 --> 00:04:49.570
This should happen every layer
of your experiences, back-end,

00:04:49.570 --> 00:04:51.790
front-end, and APIs.

00:04:51.790 --> 00:04:53.440
We discussed Gherkin
as a great way

00:04:53.440 --> 00:04:56.020
to document both the
requirements and a test

00:04:56.020 --> 00:04:57.820
scenario at one time.

00:04:57.820 --> 00:05:01.600
This smart way of writing
saves a ton of team time

00:05:01.600 --> 00:05:04.700
and helps enable
everyone to weigh in.

00:05:04.700 --> 00:05:07.090
Furthermore, Gherkin can
be converted directly

00:05:07.090 --> 00:05:11.530
into programmatic test
scripts, saving even more time.

00:05:11.530 --> 00:05:16.030
Fourth, automate testing but
don't avoid manual testing.

00:05:16.030 --> 00:05:18.580
We discussed on
your CI/CD pipeline

00:05:18.580 --> 00:05:20.950
can assist in quality
assurance processes

00:05:20.950 --> 00:05:24.730
by standardized testing,
deployment, and integration.

00:05:24.730 --> 00:05:27.880
But don't solely rely
on automated testing.

00:05:27.880 --> 00:05:30.040
Your team should
always get involved

00:05:30.040 --> 00:05:32.920
and conduct manual tests
to validate the automated

00:05:32.920 --> 00:05:35.290
testing is working properly.

00:05:35.290 --> 00:05:38.440
Fifth, test early and often.

00:05:38.440 --> 00:05:42.730
Quality is about consistently
delivering quality experiences.

00:05:42.730 --> 00:05:46.120
Your code, designed APIs,
and user experiences

00:05:46.120 --> 00:05:48.430
should constantly be
reviewed and supported

00:05:48.430 --> 00:05:51.350
to ensure continuous
quality assurance.

00:05:51.350 --> 00:05:53.720
Testing in each sprint right
after code is developed

00:05:53.720 --> 00:05:56.630
is a great way to catch bugs
before they are a larger

00:05:56.630 --> 00:05:57.800
impact.

00:05:57.800 --> 00:06:00.110
Oftentimes, the QA
and the developer

00:06:00.110 --> 00:06:03.080
will sit side by side together
at the end of their sprint

00:06:03.080 --> 00:06:05.270
to do a QA walkthrough.

00:06:05.270 --> 00:06:06.980
If something's
found, the developer

00:06:06.980 --> 00:06:10.250
will fix it on the spot,
and no defect ticket even

00:06:10.250 --> 00:06:12.010
needs to be logged.

00:06:12.010 --> 00:06:16.480
Finally, and sixth, include
your customers in the process.

00:06:16.480 --> 00:06:19.120
Your customers are and
developer community

00:06:19.120 --> 00:06:21.350
can help ensure quality.

00:06:21.350 --> 00:06:24.110
Invite them to a user testing
at the end of the sprint

00:06:24.110 --> 00:06:27.830
or have them play with an alpha
or beta version of your APIs.

00:06:27.830 --> 00:06:30.800
Building a pilot
customer group can be one

00:06:30.800 --> 00:06:33.560
of your most valuable assets.

00:06:33.560 --> 00:06:37.640
Listen to what they have to say
and issues they report to you.

00:06:37.640 --> 00:06:40.880
Everyone should be involved
with the quality assurance.

00:06:40.880 --> 00:06:44.150
Hopefully, you've found a few
strategies in the presentation

00:06:44.150 --> 00:06:46.160
to help build a successful
quality assurance

00:06:46.160 --> 00:06:50.420
strategy to support your
APIs and ongoing development

00:06:50.420 --> 00:06:52.860
and customer experiences.

00:06:52.860 --> 00:06:54.950
If you want more
information, check out

00:06:54.950 --> 00:06:57.620
the community for
ebooks, articles,

00:06:57.620 --> 00:06:59.750
and other related topics.

00:06:59.750 --> 00:07:00.950
Thank you for watching.

00:07:00.950 --> 00:07:04.300
[MUSIC PLAYING]

